{id:'mc-capm-ols', type:'mc', channel:'capm', ch_label:'CAPM as ML',
 text:'CAPM is estimated via OLS: <strong>r_s = α + β·r_m + ε</strong>. This is mathematically identical to <code>hedge_ratio(y, x)</code> in <code>pairs.py</code>. What is the only structural difference?',
